{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/868874-standard-bearers-in-the-army-of-darkness-legion-hack-brainstorming","id":868874,"title":"Standard-Bearers in the Army of Darkness [\"Legion\" Hack Brainstorming]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-19T16:18:32-07:00","id":868874,"title":"Standard-Bearers in the Army of Darkness [\"Legion\" Hack Brainstorming]","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/820371-portraying-beast-as-inferno?p=833927#post833927\">A while back</a> I made offhand mention of trying to sort out a Beast systems hack to change Lair to Legion; I've not gotten much further now than I was then, but I figured I'd put what notes I have up in case anyone cares to offer their input and/or borrow from what's here.<br /> <br /> One of the biggest things, evidently, is that decentralizing Lair means Lair Traits need adjusted or replaced to account for the shift in focus. We'll come back to that.<br /> <br /> Another thing, obviously, is the matter of Chambers \u2014 the chief replacement that comes to mind for those is something like prototypes or elite units or similar iconic characters whose qualities inform the uses of whatever Lair Traits are converted to.<br /> <br /> It probably goes without saying, but one of the effects of this hack is that Kinship and Lair resonance effectively switch places in terms of prominence and diversity of effects. Given this and the loss of Chambers, we can probably shuffle the effects of Under the Bed to serve as a territory-marker mechanic rather than generating a shortcut to the Dream; the normal means of generating Chambers can then be similarly shuffled to &quot;recruiting&quot; some new monster to your Legion.<br /> <br /> Heightened focus on Kinship suggests that Lair Traits might do well being flipped, in a sense; perhaps major Traits include supernatural templates and your starting pair must include at least one major Trait.<br /> <br /> This is an incredibly rough sketch at the moment, but if anybody has any ideas or comments or questions about this shenanigan, feel free to speak up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T19:54:59-07:00","id":869029,"title":"","content":"I have wanted to see more of Beasts as the keystone of a supernatural nexus or the head of a more tightly-tied family of monsters, but I hadn't considered a hack with this far-reaching consequences. Could be interesting.<br /> <br /> I wonder if Lair Traits could be substituted by something that heavily influences the shape of the Beast's power depending on the particular Chamber-equivalent they are tied to - the supernatural template possessed by the extension of your Legion, as you suggested, or something else supernaturally defining about the character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T21:07:44-07:00","id":1194435,"title":"","content":"Bumping this thread in light of the Player's Guide having rules for Primordial Cults (which are one-per-Beast) led by Horror-marked Heralds (who take on subtle physical quirks inspired by their Beasts and the supernatural qualities their investiture).<br /> <br /> It may be necessary to work out a less granular means of representing some of these things for this hack, because the available mechanics mostly lean into Beast's greater emphasis on Merits and thematic anchors.<br /> <br /> Or we could also lean into it, I suppose. Doubling down on the proliferation of Supernatural Merits, perhaps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}